# Sameward rebrand / infrastructure policy

Brand: **Sameward**. Primary domain: **sameward.com**.

Goal: user-facing product is Sameward. Existing internal infrastructure stays stable unless there is a real technical/business reason to migrate.

## Do

- Keep product UI, copy, logos, metadata, emails, and marketing as Sameward
- Name **new** resources with Sameward conventions (`sameward-…`, `SAMEWARD_…`)
- Keep docs accurate to real infrastructure names
- Treat future renames as dedicated migrations (backup → migrate → verify → rollback path)

## Do not

- Migrate MongoDB `dbName: "teamhub"`, Atlas cluster hostname, S3 bucket/IAM, env/secret names, AWS/deploy identifiers, or OpenAI config purely for branding
- Change docs to pretend infrastructure is named Sameward when it is not
- Chase “zero occurrences of teamhub” — that is not the objective
- Recreate Google OAuth client IDs/secrets for branding; only verify consent-screen branding for production
- Block product work on optional GitHub repo rename (`teamhub-ai` → `sameward`)

## When classifying leftover `teamhub` references

- **A** User-facing / must change → flag and fix
- **B** Existing internal infrastructure → leave alone
- **C** Docs accurately describing existing infra → leave alone
- **D** Optional future cleanup → mention only; do not change unless asked

Only start an infrastructure migration when the user explicitly asks, or a genuine technical requirement requires it.

## Chat / workspace scope

This repo and its Agent chats are **Sameward / TeamHub product work only**.

Portfolio redesign lives in `~/Desktop/new_portfolio_2026/portfolio-2026` — open a separate chat there. Do not implement portfolio UI/3D work in Sameward chats.
